-- A `gen { … }` block (#109): a generator written in place, whose body captures what it uses
-- (`k` here). It yields `k` and `k + 1` and finishes with `()`. It is elaborated as a `gen fn`'s
-- body is, to one state machine (SPEC §15) whose first state holds what the block captures, and
-- whose `close` there drops it; the block runs nothing until it is observed. `gen-block.core.bc`
-- is its elaboration in core, as `bcc desugar` prints it.
-- Answer: i32[7], 3 + 4.

main -> i32 =
  let k = 3;
  let mut acc = 0;
  for x in gen { yield k; yield k + 1 } { acc = acc + x };
  acc
